   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I googled &quot;round_any() ggplot&quot; and the first page that popped up was <a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org/0.9.3.1/geom_boxplot.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.ggplot2.org/0.9.3.1/geom_boxplot.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369696885000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Jkn_1fjIQtbQFpUi_us-9\">http://docs.ggplot2.org/0.9.3.1/geom_boxplot.html</a><div><br></div><div>If I ctrl+f to &quot;round_any()&quot; it says:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;font-size:12.0249996185303px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"># Scales vs. coordinate transforms -------\r\n# Scale transformations occur before the boxplot statistics are computed.\r\n# Coordinate transformations occur afterwards.  Observe the effect on the\r\n# number of outliers.\r\nlibrary(plyr) # to access round_any\r\nm &lt;- ggplot(movies, aes(y = votes, x = rating,\r\n   group = round_any(rating, 0.5)))\r\nm + geom_boxplot()</span><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;font-size:12.0249996185303px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:12.0249996185303px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">In short, you need to load the plyr package to be able to use this function.</font></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:12.0249996185303px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:12.0249996185303px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font 