     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jan 28, 2015 at 4:21 PM, Roman Luštrik <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">roman....@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I could plot/calculate the rounded number by calling the variable explicitly (movies$).<div><br></div><div>ggplot(movies, aes(y = votes, x = rating, group = round_any(movies$rating, 0.5))) + geom_boxplot()<br></div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Roman</div><div><br></div></div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jan 28, 2015 at 4:19 PM, Troels Ring <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tr...@gvdnet.dk</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n  \r\n    \r\n  \r\n  <div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\">\r\n    Sorry:<br>\r\n     qplot(year, budget, data = movies, geom = &quot;boxplot&quot;,<br>\r\n       group = round_any(year, 10, floor)) #Fejl i eval(expr, envir,\r\n    enclos) : could not find function &quot;round_any&quot;<br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    Best wishes<div><div><br>\r\n    Troels<br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    <div>Den 28-01-2015 kl. 15:16 skrev Roman\r\n      Luštrik:<br>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n      <div dir=\"ltr\">I googled &quot;round_any() ggplot&quot; and the first page\r\n        that popped up was <a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org/0.9.3.1/geom_boxplot.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.ggplot2.org/0.9.3.1/geom_boxplot.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369696894000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0zjayl6ywN_rSi25IY5Fkl\">http://docs.ggplot2.org/0.9.3.1/geom_boxplot.html</a>\r\n        <div><br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div>If I ctrl+f to &quot;round_any()&quot; it says:</div>\r\n        <div><br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div><span>#\r\n            Scales vs. coordinate transforms -------\r\n            # Scale transformations occur before the boxplot statistics\r\n            are computed.\r\n            # Coordinate transformations occur afterwards. Observe the\r\n            effect on the\r\n            # number of outliers.\r\n            library(plyr) # to access round_any\r\n            m &lt;- ggplot(movies, aes(y = votes, x = rating, group =\r\n            round_any(rating, 0.5)))\r\n            m + geom_boxplot()</span><br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div><span><br>\r\n          </span></div>\r\n        <div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:12.0249996185303px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">In short, you need to\r\n              load the plyr package to be able to use this function.</font></span></div>\r\n        <div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:12.0249996185303px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br>\r\n            </font></span></div>\r\n        <div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:12.0249996185303px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Cheers,</font></span></div>\r\n        <div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:12.0249996185303px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Roman</font></span></div>\r\n        <div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:12.0249996185303px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br>\r\n            </font></span></div>\r\n        <div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:12.0249996185303px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br>\r\n            </font></span></div>\r\n      </div>\r\n      <div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br>\r\n        <div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jan 28, 2015 at 2:57 PM, Troels\r\n          Ring <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tr...@gvdnet.dk</a>&gt;</span>\r\n          wrote:<br>\r\n          <blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n            <div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, sorry to ask simple questions, but in the\r\n              ggplot2 book on p 71 an example uses a founction\r\n              round_any() - which not seems to be known. Any solutions?\r\n              <div>All best wishes</div>\r\n              <div><br>\r\n              </div>\r\n              <div>Troels</div>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n                -- <br>\r\n                -- <br>\r\n                You received this message because you are subscribed to\r\n                the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\n                Please provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369696894000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2A6wXe4xFNi2oSvMsi31Za\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>\r\n                 <br>\r\n                To post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n                To unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n                More options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369696894000&amp;usg=AOvVaw287ODcwFPPsOGMPjbwskSq\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a><br>\r\n                <br>\r\n                --- <br>\r\n                You received this message because you are subscribed to\r\n                the Google Groups &quot;ggplot2&quot; group.<br>\r\n                To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails\r\n                from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n                For more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369696894000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ohbWBNgjkLYAIYNkwPx0_\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n              </font></span></blockquote>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <br>\r\n        <br clear=\"all\">\r\n        <div><br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        -- <br>\r\n        <div>In God we trust, all others bring\r\n          data.</div>\r\n      </div>\r\n      -- <br>\r\n      -- <br>\r\n      You received this message because you are subscribed to the\r\n      ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\n      Please provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369696894000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2A6wXe4xFNi2oSvMsi31Za\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>\r\n       <br>\r\n      To post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n      To unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n      More options: <a href=\"http://groups.google